  <metadata>
    <name>Langdale and Elterwater Long Round</name>
    <desc>28.7 km with 232 m of climb. From the Bracken Fell Harriers route book.</desc>
  </metadata>
  <trk>
    <name>Langdale and Elterwater Long Round</name>
    <desc>Our long steady one: valley tracks and bridleways linking Elterwater, Great Langdale, Little Langdale and Skelwith. Nothing steep and nowhere technical — just honest distance with the Langdale Pikes for company the whole way round. Two sensible exit points if the day stops being fun.</desc>
